=== trade-reconstruction vs archived order books (OddPool) ===
  what this underwrites: 8,024 of 10,069 Kalshi game prices (80%) are
  reconstructed from the trade tape rather than read off a quoted book
  validated sample: 98 games (99 fetched, 1 with no archived book)

  exact bid match: 94.9%   exact ask match: 96.9%
  |mid error|: mean 0.43pt, median 0.00pt, within 1pt: 99.0%
  archived snapshot gap to official start: median 0.5 min

    league     n  mean |mid err|    median  within 1pt
     CBB-M    38           0.00pt     0.00pt      100.0%
       MLB    11           0.05pt     0.00pt      100.0%
       NBA    24           1.67pt     0.00pt       95.8%
       NHL    25           0.06pt     0.00pt      100.0%

  COVERAGE LIMIT: no validated rows for CFB, NFL, WNBA. The
  reconstruction is a per-market mechanism, not a league-specific one, but
  the report must say the validation does not cover these leagues directly.

  Read: the reconstruction recovers the archived touch almost exactly. The
  residual is concentrated in NBA, the league whose books move fastest
  between the last fill and the bell. robustness_cuts section 2 shows the
  three-way verdict is the same on recon-priced and book-mid-priced games.
